# ClarityOS — Cline Project Rules

## BFF Pattern (Next.js → FastAPI)
- All JSON API calls from the frontend go through `app/api/` BFF routes using `proxyToFastAPI()` from `@/lib/bff`
- FastAPI upstream URLs MUST have a trailing slash: `/api/payers/` not `/api/payers`
- **EXCEPTION — PDF binary routes**: do NOT use `proxyToFastAPI()` for binary responses. Use raw `fetch()` + `res.arrayBuffer()` + `new NextResponse(buffer, { headers: { "Content-Type": "application/pdf" } })`. `proxyToFastAPI()` corrupts binary.

## SQLAlchemy (Python)
- NEVER call `db.refresh()` after `db.flush()` — it throws `MissingGreenlet` in async context
- Always re-fetch with `selectinload` after flush:
  ```python
  result = await db.execute(select(Model).where(Model.id == obj.id).options(selectinload(Model.relation)))
  obj = result.scalar_one()
  ```
- Enum columns: always `native_enum=False` (store as VARCHAR, not PG enum type)
- Decimal fields: always `float(val)` before passing to reportlab or arithmetic — never pass raw `Decimal`

## Frontend Components
- `components/` are presentational only — no `fetch()` calls, no DB access, no business logic
- State goes in Zustand stores under `store/`
- Imports: always use `@/` path alias, never relative (`../../`) imports
- Glass CSS classes (from globals.css): `.glass-card`, `.glass-input`, `.glass-card-hover`

## Zustand Stores
- Always use 3-argument `set()`, `devtools` middleware, and a `{ name: "storeName" }` devtools label
- Export selector hooks: `usePayerStore`, `useBillingStore` (not raw store object)

## FastAPI Router Registration
- `/fee-catalog` routes MUST be registered BEFORE `/{payer_id}` in the payer router — order matters
- Check `backend/api/main.py` for existing `include_router` calls before adding new ones at the same prefix
- If `/api/patients` already has a router with a `/{patient_id}` catch-all, add new sub-routes to THAT file — do NOT add a second `include_router` at the same prefix

## General Rules
- Never add npm or pip packages without user approval — check if an existing dep can do it first
- Never log patient data — not even `console.log` in dev
- `@/` alias always — check `tsconfig.json` `paths` if unsure
- Auth middleware is required on every clinical route — never add an unguarded endpoint
